  "sn45.161:0.1": "Linked Discourses 45.161 ",
  "sn45.161:0.2": "13. Searches ",
  "sn45.161:0.3": "Searches ",
  "sn45.161:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn45.161:1.2": "“Mendicants, there are these three searches. ",
  "sn45.161:1.3": "What three? ",
  "sn45.161:1.4": "The search for sensual pleasures, the search for continued existence, and the search for a spiritual path. ",
  "sn45.161:1.5": "These are the three searches. ",
  "sn45.161:1.6": "The noble eightfold path should be developed to directly know these three searches. ",
  "sn45.161:1.7": "What is the noble eightfold path? ",
  "sn45.161:1.8": "It’s when a mendicant develops right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right immersion, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go. ",
  "sn45.161:1.9": "This is the noble eightfold path that should be developed to directly know these three searches.” ",
  "sn45.161:2.1": "“Mendicants, there are these three searches. ",
  "sn45.161:2.2": "What three? ",
